---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import UVScale from '../components/UVScale.astro';
import EvidenceNote from '../components/EvidenceNote.astro';
import StoreButton from '../components/StoreButton.astro';
import { SITE, absoluteUrl, organizationSchema } from '../config';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: SITE.name,
    applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'iOS',
    url: absoluteUrl('/'),
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      price: '0',
      priceCurrency: 'USD',
    },
    downloadUrl: SITE.appStoreUrl,
    publisher: organizationSchema(),
  },
  organizationSchema(),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  path="/"
  title="Bronzla · Know your safe time in the sun"
  description="Bronzla works out how long you can safely stay in the sun today, from the current UV index, your Fitzpatrick skin type and your SPF. Free on the App Store, no ads, no subscription, no in-app purchases."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Hero locale="en" />

  <section class="container feature feature-text">
    <h2>A number, not a guess</h2>
    <p>
      "Stay out of the midday sun" is advice nobody can actually follow. Bronzla replaces it with
      a number: the minutes you have today, worked out from the UV index where you are, your
      Fitzpatrick skin type and the SPF you're wearing. It caps every recommendation at 60 per
      cent of the calculated burn time and never suggests more than three hours, whatever the
      arithmetic says.
    </p>
    <p>
      A seven-question quiz determines your Fitzpatrick type without asking you to eyeball a
      chart. The questions are written for the olive and wheat tones common along the
      Mediterranean and Aegean coasts, on their own terms rather than against northern European
      reference points.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/science/">Read the full method and citation list</a>
  </section>

  <section class="container feature feature-list">
    <h2>Timer</h2>
    <p class="feature-intro">
      Flip and sunscreen reminders that work with the phone in your bag and the screen off. The
      remaining time stays live on your lock screen.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <h3>Flip reminder</h3>
        <p>A nudge to turn, so both sides get an even dose through the session.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Sunscreen reminder</h3>
        <p>A prompt to reapply every two hours, sooner after swimming or towelling.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Live on the lock screen</h3>
        <p>The countdown keeps running and stays visible without unlocking the phone.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="container uv-section">
    <h2>UV forecast</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Hourly and ten day UV forecasts, with the riskiest hours of the day called out plainly, so
      you can see a burn coming before you leave the house. Every reading maps to the same five
      WHO bands the app uses everywhere else, coloured to rise in luminance with severity so the
      scale still reads correctly for colour vision deficiency.
    </p>
    <UVScale locale="en" />
  </section>

  <section class="container evidence-section">
    <h2>Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <EvidenceNote locale="en" />
    <a class="text-link" href="/science/">See the full method, worked examples and sources</a>
  </section>

  <section class="container privacy-section">
    <h2>No account, because there is nowhere to send your data</h2>
    <p>
      There is no server behind Bronzla. Your skin type, your session history and your tan
      tracker photos stay in local storage on your phone. Location is used only to ask Apple
      WeatherKit for the UV index where you are; it is never linked to an identity, and you can
      skip it entirely and pick a city instead. No analytics SDK, no advertising, no third party
      of any kind.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the full privacy page</a>
  </section>

  <section class="container closing-cta">
    <h2>Free. No ads, no subscription, no in-app purchases.</h2>
    <StoreButton locale="en" size="large" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .feature {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .feature-text {
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .feature-text p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .feature-list {
    max-width: 960px;
  }

  .feature-intro {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  /*
   * A deliberate row, not a stacked column: three sub-items sit side by side above a
   * hairline divider on wide viewports, separated by hairline rules rather than boxed
   * into cards (DESIGN.md bans the identical icon-card grid; this is plain type).
   * Below 640px there isn't room for three columns, so the divider rotates to sit
   * above each item instead of beside it.
   */
  .feature-list ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .feature-list li {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem 0;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .feature-list li:first-child {
    padding-left: 0;
    border-left: none;
  }

  .feature-list p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .feature-list ul {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      border-top: none;
    }

    .feature-list li {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
      border-left: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    }

    .feature-list li:first-child {
      padding-left: 0;
      border-top: none;
    }
  }

  .uv-section,
  .evidence-section,
  .privacy-section {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .section-lede {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .privacy-section p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .closing-cta {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .closing-cta h2 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
</style>
